## Why This Is Asked

Tests stateful per-key windowing, dynamic rule handling, and exactly-once guarantees under late messages.

## Key Concepts
- Per-account sliding window sums
- Dynamic rule lookup and on-the-fly threshold changes
- Watermarks for late arrivals and eviction
- Exactly-once semantics and idempotent fraud_alerts
- Backpressure and test canary design

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: per-account rolling sum with 5m sliding window
state = Map(); // accountId -> [{ts, amt}]
rules = Map(); // accountId -> threshold
onEvent(tx) {
  cleanExpired(tx.ts);
  sum = sumAmt(state.get(tx.accountId));
  threshold = rules.get(tx.accountId) ?? default;
  if (sum > threshold) emitFraud(tx.accountId, sum, threshold);
  append(state, tx.accountId, {ts: tx.ts, amt: tx.amount});
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle simultaneous rule updates and transactions to avoid inconsistent alerts?
- How would you scale to millions of accounts and high-throughput streams while maintaining low latency?

## Why This Is Asked
Privacy-first multi-tenant KCNA is a real challenge; rotation and audit are painful at scale.

## Key Concepts
- Envelope encryption
- Per-tenant KMS keys
- On-the-fly rotation with no downtime
- Audit trails and access control
- Backward compatibility with legacy envelopes
- Canary tests for rotation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: envelope encrypt data per tenant
function encryptForTenant(tenantId, plaintext, version) {
  const keyId = kms.getKeyId(tenantId, version);
  const dataKey = kms.generateDataKey(tenantId, version);
  const ciphertext = crypto.aesGcmEncrypt(dataKey.plaintext, plaintext);
  const envelope = { keyId, cipher: ciphertext, iv: dataKey.iv };
  return envelope;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How to handle key compromise and revocation?
- How to measure rotation latency and impact on throughput?
- How to ensure consistent decryption across hot/cold storage?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design real-time access control in a multi-tenant KCNA deployment with minimal downtime and strong auditability.

## Key Concepts
