## Why This Is Asked

This question probes ability to design a scalable, auditable governance layer that operates within strict per-tenant boundaries while maintaining low latency in KCNA's streaming pipeline.

## Key Concepts

- Policy representation: graph-based rules, versioned, tenant-scoped
- Real-time evaluation: per-record decisions, caching, cache invalidation
- Privacy vs. usefulness: field-level masking vs. full redaction
- Auditability: tamper-evident logs, provenance tagging, verifiable proofs

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: evaluatePolicy(tenantId, topic, record) -> { maskFields: [..], sinks: [..], tags: [..] }
function evaluatePolicy(tenantId, topic, record) {
  const policy = policyCache.get(tenantId, topic);
  // apply masking rules
  for (const f of policy.maskFields) {
    if (record.hasOwnProperty(f)) record[f] = mask(record[f]);
  }
  // attach provenance tags
  record._tags = policy.tags;
  return { masked: record, sinks: policy.sinks };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle policy drift during upgrades without downtime?
- How do you prove policy adherence during audits across backups and restores?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to join across topics with late-arriving updates, implement a TTL-based in-memory state store, and maintain at-least-once semantics while isolating enrichment logic.

## Key Concepts
- Cross-topic enrichment and per-key state
- TTL-based eviction and stale data handling
- Out-of-order arrival tolerance and idempotent processing
- Error routing to dead_letters and offset management

## Code Example
```javascript
// Skeleton: in-memory profile store with TTL
class ProfileStore {
  constructor(ttlMs) { this.ttlMs = ttlMs; this.map = new Map(); }
  update(userId, profile) { this.map.set(userId, { profile, t: Date.now() }); }
  get(userId) {
    const e = this.map.get(userId); if (!e) return null;
    if (Date.now() - e.t > this.ttlMs) { this.map.delete(userId); return null; }
    return e.profile;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test eviction and data freshness without data loss?
- How would you simulate out-of-order profile updates in tests?
